            <ArticleTitle>Migraine, daily chronic headache and fibromyalgia in the same patient: an evolutive &quot;continuum&quot; of non organic chronic pain? About 100 clinical cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S291-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aim of this study is to evaluate if migraine, daily chronic headache and fibromyalgia in the same patient can be considered as an evolutive continuum of non organic chronic pain. Therefore, migraine, daily chronic headache and fibromyalgia should be considered the expression of chronic antinociceptive system alteration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
